title: Shai-Hulud npm Worm - Preinstall Hook Credential Harvesting
id: 7c9e1f3a-5b2d-4a8c-6e0f-3d7b9a1c5e8f
status: experimental
description: Detects npm packages executing preinstall lifecycle hooks that run 'bun run index.js' or similar credential-harvesting payloads. The Shai-Hulud worm uses this mechanism to automatically execute malware when developers or CI/CD pipelines install affected dependencies.
references:
  - https://gbhackers.com/known-npm-worm-returns-after-111-days-and-security-scanning-still-let-it-through/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-08
tags:
  - attack.t1195
  - attack.t1059
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: linux
detection:
  selection_bun:
    Image|endswith: '/bun'
    CommandLine|contains: 'run'
    CommandLine|contains: 'index.js'
  selection_npm_preinstall:
    Image|endswith: '/npm'
    CommandLine|contains: 'preinstall'
    CommandLine|contains: 'bun'
  selection_credential_harvest:
    CommandLine|contains: 'npm_token'
    OR CommandLine|contains: 'github_token'
    OR CommandLine|contains: 'ssh_keyscan'
    OR CommandLine|contains: 'docker_config'
  condition: (selection_bun and selection_credential_harvest) or selection_npm_preinstall
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate bun-based development workflows running index.js (unlikely with credential keywords)
level: high
